@node requirements "Requirements"
Historically ixprefs runs under AmigaOS 2.04 or later and p.OS;
the GUI is provided for AmigaOS.  The original program needs at
least ixemul.library v47.

The new 80.3 I/O settings and tagged preferences require matching
80.3-era library and ixprefs sources.  Do not use an 80.3 tagged
preferences file with ixemul.library 80.2 or earlier.

ixprefscheck 1.0 is a separate C89-compatible utility.  It operates
on a named 28-byte preferences file and does not call ixemul's
settings APIs.  A native GCC build may still link against ixemul
as its normal C runtime, so it is not guaranteed to execute if the
installed C runtime cannot initialize.

For the updated native sources, use GeekGadgets GCC 2.95.3 or a
compatible AmigaOS C environment.  Native compiler and runtime
verification of the new tools remains the responsibility of the
AmigaOS build/test environment.
@endnode
@node acknowledgments "Acknowledgments"
Kamil Iskra (iskra@student.uci.agh.edu.pl) made several enhancement
suggestions and contributed code for adapting ixprefs to AmigaOS 3.x
(see program @{"history" link history}).

Hans Verkuil (hans@wyst.hobby.nl) was kind enough to consider integrating
ixprefs with ixemul.library, and to let me know in advance of the changes he
planned to make to the library, so that I could adapt ixprefs on time.
Hans also updated ixprefs from version 2.0 beta 4 to 2.1, and has also
updated the program to versions 2.2, 2.3, 2.4 and 2.5.

Thanks to Martin Blom (lcs@lysator.liu.se) for pointing out that I had to use
EraseRect() to visually erase a gadget from a window.
@endnode
